    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The inclusion criteria were: (1) Conformed to research questions, i.e., studies that estimated the reinfection rate of SARS-CoV-2 or we could calculate it based on the data provided in the paper; (2) The study design included cohort study, case-control study, and descriptive study; (3) The study fited our working definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection. ... The exclusion criteria were: (1) The sample size was less than 20; (2) Belonged to one of the following types of studies: editorial, case report, case series study, systematic review, meta-analysis, animal experiment, news report; (3) Secondary reporting or articles on repeated studies of the same population; (4) Grey literature, including a range of documents not controlled by commercial publishing organizations.",
      "reason": "Specifies study characteristics including research questions, eligible study designs, and follow-up requirements (90-day interval)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "To avoid language bias, the search was not limited to any language. ... The exclusion criteria were: ... (4) Grey literature, including a range of documents not controlled by commercial publishing organizations.",
      "reason": "Specifies language (no restriction) and publication status (excludes grey literature), but dissemination year is not mentioned."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "One of them reported only the reinfection rate, but not the associated number of first infections as well as the number of reinfections, and two other articles studied the same population, so the meta-analysis of single-group rates could not be performed. Therefore, we excluded the above literature with the number of unreported infections",
      "reason": "Mentions exclusion due to unreported outcome results, but does not explicitly distinguish from outcomes not measured."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Subgroup analyses were performed for age, reinfection variant, country, study population, and study type respectively, and the results were shown in Table 1",
      "reason": "Specifies groups used in synthesis and links to review objectives of examining rates in different regions and populations."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_19",
      "quote": "we did not include the 'grey literature', which may lack potential relevant studies that meet the inclusion criteria",
      "reason": "Rationale provided for excluding grey literature, but not for other restrictions like sample size or study types."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
